      "dateCreated": "",
      "description": "Identifies high-frequency aptamer candidate sequences from paired-end FASTQ files produced by SELEX experiments. Runs three sequential filtering stages — (1) matching/orientation by left and right constant regions within a mismatch tolerance, (2) exact-match flanking marker extraction, and (3) random-region (N) extraction requiring exact stems and an exact between-length — followed by aggregation that counts identical survivors and ranks them by descending count with first-seen tie-breaking. R1 and R2 are each treated as their own sequence and pooled per stage. All pattern sequences, mismatch tolerances and lengths are user-configurable; the overall insert length is derived automatically.",
